  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "UK politics live: Burnham says he wants to fight next election on plan for new taxes to pay for free social care in England",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2026/sep/27/uk-politics-live-labour-party-conference-andy-burnham-angela-rayner-latest-news-updates",
      "description": "<p>PM appears to be anticipating criticism of reforms that he will set out on Tuesday at the Labour party conference</p><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/sep/26/burnham-pledges-radical-change-labour-conference-exclusive\">‘I can deliver’: Burnham pledges radical change on eve of Labour conference</a></p><p><strong>Kuenssberg</strong> puts it to Burnham that, according to the Health Foundation, a system offering adult social care free at the point of delivery (like healthcare delivered by the NHS) would cost £18bn.</p><p><strong>Burnham</strong> says the cost is “not that high” (ie, not as high as £18bn).</p><p>Not that high.</p><p>But can I directly deal with this issue of the costs?</p><p>Louise Casey is still doing an official review for us, so I will set out the vision, if you like, on Tuesday [in his speech to the conference].</p><p>Louise will then help us with the how. How do we make this happen? When can we make it happen?</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2026/sep/27/uk-politics-live-labour-party-conference-andy-burnham-angela-rayner-latest-news-updates\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-27T15:39:55"
    },
    {
      "title": "Burnham refreshes the parts others can’t reach on the Andy and Laura show | John Crace",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/sep/27/andy-burnham-laura-kuenssberg-show-social-care",
      "description": "<p>The PM oozes confidence and easy-going charm as he tells Laura Kuenssberg the hill he’ll die on is fixing social care</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2026/sep/27/uk-politics-live-labour-party-conference-andy-burnham-angela-rayner-latest-news-updates\">UK politics live – latest updates</a></p></li></ul><p>In recent weeks there has been much speculation in some parts of the media that Andy Burnham would be calling an early general election. Speculation that existed largely in the heads of those writing the stories, as even the most favourable polls suggest that Labour would lose its huge majority and become the largest party in a coalition government. But to stop the chatter dominating his party conference, Burnham made it clear there would be no early election. His reward? Headlines in the rightwing press that he had bottled it. By not calling an election he had never planned to call. Sometimes you just can’t win.</p><p>There again, you might call this a first-world problem for the prime minister. This time last year, Burnham had been hanging around the fringes of the conference as he and his allies attempted one of the most half-arsed coups in living memory. One that fizzled out almost before it had started and became the butt of many jokes among Keir Starmer’s inner circle. Andy looked to have blown himself up on the runway, leaving Keir safe for the duration of the parliament.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/sep/27/andy-burnham-laura-kuenssberg-show-social-care\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-27T15:17:23"
    }
  ]
